  "operatorObservations": [
    "A separate dedicated headless Chrome profile was launched with --mute-audio and used only the owned localhost4248 testing page. Every DOM inspection reported muted sound and a stable1100x850 viewport with800x600 native canvas.",
    "Actual current native starting20 and40 saves were imported through the reload controls. The ZIP members were byte-checked against their separately generated native fixture manifests before import.",
    "Each active window freshly imported its starting fixture; native Continue and speed-button inputs established the scene, and the native Menu paused gameplay while the local form was prepared.",
    "Native DOM form selection declared the exact crowd,speed,phase,probe mode and15second interval before every arm. Inside the2second arm delay, active windows resumed through Back To Game and captured their start image; no input was sent throughout the measurement.",
    "All four start/end active images show an active night lawn at the declared native1x or2x speed. Populations and plants evolved naturally; none of the windows earned a browser win. Top-row Fume heads visibly overlap seed packets as they reach the left, recorded as a presentation observation rather than a bounds-pass assertion.",
    "The paused native and raf-only windows share the same freshly imported20starting save and stayed in the native Menu throughout. No native game input was sent between the paired controls; their start screenshots are byte-identical.",
    "All six raw reports passed recorder preconditions on their first measurement. Raw reports and12actual JPEGs are preserved, with no outlier deletion, threshold change,or measurement retry.",
    "Before any measurement,the original char-key controller could not edit the DOM label because native SDL intercepted typing. Its source and transcript were preserved; root approved a restricted native IME text helper and triple-click for only the visible performance-label field. The exact same owned paused page was reconnected,with transition source hashes recorded.",
    "The last recorded action successfully closed the page. This evidence measures native callback CPU,full synchronous save capture CPU and requestAnimationFrame scheduling; it makes no GPU timing or presented-frame FPS claim."
  ],
